// Halden Reach, read off its walls (NAR-15, docs/story/environment.md). An anchored city: its things say the
// same thing forever, which is the point. The thing speaks, never a person; reading changes nothing. The catalog
// is `Dressing`. The orchard's gravestone is `Orchard_Gravestone`.

title: Bridges_TollBoard
---
Board: Tolls of the Seven Bridges. Revised each spring, by order of the Crown. #still #line:0166539
Board: Forty springs of revisions below it. Every figure matches the one above. #plant:5.1 #still #line:07e5c09
===

title: Mills_Sheets
---
Sheet: New vellum, hung to dry. A flaw in one corner: a thumbprint pressed into the pulp. #still #line:021d672
Sheet: The next sheet has it too. And the next. The whole loft has the same thumb. #plant:5.1 #still #line:031eca3
===

title: Hall_Roll
---
Roll: Guildmasters of the Meridian, cut in the stone. Nine names, and a tenth. #still #line:02abad2
Roll: The ninth is chiselled out. The owl's-eye crest beside it was left. #plant:5.4 #still #line:067c320
Roll: The tenth is Aurelian Voss. The stone under him is smooth. #still #line:043cfda
===

title: Hall_Order
---
Notice: By the Guildmaster's order. No Warden crosses the Greyfold line. No tether is issued for the Old Capital. #still #line:0c93279
Notice: No exceptions. No requests. The paper is forty years old. The pins are new. #plant:5.5 #still #line:04a8a37
===

title: Hall_ExamPapers
---
Papers: An exam on every desk. Question one: "Name the seven bridges of Halden, in order." #still #line:0bfd52a
Papers: The same paper on every desk. The date at the top is forty years old. The ink is wet. #plant:5.1 #still #line:0d45777
===

title: Lowmarket_Notice
---
Notice: SURVEY SCHEDULED. By order of the Meridian Guild. #still #line:04c2dd1
Notice: Under it, older notices, each saying the same. The bottom one is brown. #still #line:0ed1bfc
<<if place_fate("Halden_Lowmarket_2") == "anchored">>
    Notice: Pasted over them all, new and white: SURVEY COMPLETE. #still #line:0032e3b
<<endif>>
===

title: Bastion_Plaque
---
Plaque: The Crown's Tower. Its landing is forty wingspans up, where the old door was. #still #line:09d5aea
Plaque: This door was cut at the foot the year after the fall. There are no stairs between. #plant:5.6 #still #line:0815c81
===

title: Office_Drawing
---
Drawing: Crayon, framed. A heron as tall as the page, holding a compass. #still #line:001e9b1
Drawing: Behind him, a city, every window coloured in. In one, high up, a small heron waves. #plant:5.5 #still #line:05dd5f7
===
